From f3fce67261e417de4df11954df4a898414751738 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Voice Bot <voicebot@local>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:08:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] lakeside ambience: self-synthesized lake water + wind chime
 loop; sea waves stand down at the lakeside
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- region_lakeside/audio/amb_lake_loop.mp3 (57.8 KB, mono 24 kHz, 24 kbps CBR, 19.0 s circular loop + 0.15 s duplicate tail,
  −22.4 LUFS; pure numpy synth tools/audio/lakeside/synth_lake_amb.py, seed 20261017)
- LakeAmbienceCore (pure): wanted on lakeside state / arrival stretch / lakeside board; fade in 1.2 s, out 0.8 s; same gate
  as the beds (canPlayAmbience) and the A1c slider; two-source cross-loop at the circular period (linear 150 ms past the
  encoder delay), with the platform loop as fallback
- LakeAmbience component: loads the clip from the subpackage on first need, writes AmbienceAudio.lakeActive; registers
  mounter/quieter; [QF_AUDIO] events, [QF_LAKE] console.error on load failure (sea waves stay on)
- AmbienceAudio: lakeActive → no-world path (waves fade out, no gulls), gate log 'lakeside'; BGM unchanged (island)
- tools/test_lake_ambience.cjs (6 checks) in run-suite
